{"name":"Hubbard Squash","hex":"#e9bf8c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"squash","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sport played in a walled court with a soft rubber ball and bats like tennis racquets.","A non-alcoholic drink made from a fruit-based concentrate diluted with water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat or press into pulp or a flat mass; to crush.","To compress or restrict (oneself) into a small space; to squeeze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cucurbita maxima","blocks":[{"text":"Cucurbita maxima, one of at least five species of cultivated squash, is one of the most diverse domesticated species. This species originated in South America from the wild subspecies Cucurbita maxima subsp. andreana over 4,000 years ago. Cucurbita maxima, known for modern varieties as Hubbard, Delicious, Marblehead, Boston Marrow, and Turks Turban, originated in northern Argentina near the Andes or in certain Andean valleys. Secondary centers of diversity include India, Bangladesh, Myanmar, and the southern Appalachians."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cucurbita_maxima_Blanco2.320.png/330px-Cucurbita_maxima_Blanco2.320.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucurbita_maxima","wikidata":"Q161180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Cucurbita_maxima_subsp._andreana_compose.jpg/500px-Cucurbita_maxima_subsp._andreana_compose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Cucurbita_maxima_subsp._andreana_compose.jpg/500px-Cucurbita_maxima_subsp._andreana_compose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cucurbita maxima subsp. andreana fruits (top), plant in the middle of the season (middle) and fruits lef